      "id": "otusvvw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to High Courts"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "High Courts in India are governed under Part VI, Articles 214 to 231 of the Indian Constitution.",
        "Judges of a High Court are appointed by the President of India in consultation with the Chief Justice of India and the Governor of the concerned state.",
        "To be eligible, a candidate must be an Indian citizen with at least 10 years of judicial office or 10 years as an advocate in a High Court.",
        "Under Article 226, High Courts possess the power to issue writs for the enforcement of Fundamental Rights and for any other purpose."
      ],
      "id": "ys5bkxb"
    },
