    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "High Court writ jurisdiction under Article 226 is wider than the Supreme Court's under Article 32, as it extends to ordinary legal rights as well.",
        "The retirement age of High Court judges was increased from 60 to 62 years by the 15th Constitutional Amendment Act, 1963.",
        "Parliament holds the power to establish a common High Court for two or more states or a state and a Union Territory under Article 231."
      ],
      "id": "svlyrpn"
